Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] server: on PS5, run the completion port requests on the client threads too

Patch 0918 runs the requests that touch only sync objects, handles and file opens on the calling
thread. In a .NET (MonoGame) game the most frequent request left on the pipes was remove_completion, about 900 a
second at 15 us: .NET's thread pool takes its I/O completions from a port. NtRemoveIoCompletion asks
remove_completion, waits with select (already direct) when the port is empty, and then asks
get_thread_completion; NtSetIoCompletion asks add_completion. The four completion requests (with
query_completion) only move messages between a port's queue and its waiters, wake waiters as
event_op does, never sleep in the server, and carry handles and values, no application buffer,
so they join the list.
---
  server/request.c | 6 ++++++
  1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/server/request.c b/server/request.c
index ab127f1..aea3463 100644
--- a/server/request.c
+++ b/server/request.c
@@ -366,6 +366,12 @@ static int is_direct_request( enum request req )
     case REQ_dup_handle:
     case REQ_create_file:
     case REQ_get_handle_fd:
+    /* completion ports: queue, take and count messages, and fetch the one a
+     * wait was given; like event_op, they wake waiters and never sleep */
+    case REQ_add_completion:
+    case REQ_remove_completion:
+    case REQ_get_thread_completion:
+    case REQ_query_completion:
         return 1;
     default:
         return 0;
